        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Drag variable types into relationship maps</h2>
          <p class="lead small-lead">Rectangles represent observed variables; ovals represent latent constructs. Use the arrows and each shape's position to decide what belongs in it.</p>
          <div class="visual-alphabet" role="list" aria-label="Visual alphabet for research models">
            <article role="listitem"><span class="map-shape map-box">Rectangle</span><p><strong>Observed variable</strong><small>A concrete score, group or recorded value.</small></p></article>
            <article role="listitem"><span class="map-shape map-oval">Oval</span><p><strong>Latent variable</strong><small>An unobserved construct measured by several items.</small></p></article>
            <article role="listitem"><span class="legend-path direct-path" aria-hidden="true"></span><p><strong>Straight arrow</strong><small>Directional prediction or path coefficient.</small></p></article>
            <article role="listitem"><span class="legend-path covariance-path" aria-hidden="true"></span><p><strong>Curved double arrow</strong><small>Background covariance or correlation.</small></p></article>
          </div>
